# Scenario-tier runtime artifacts. These capture real conversations, including
# tool results that contain personal data (inbox contents, email addresses).
# Local diagnostics only — never committed; this repo is public.
tests/app/scenarios/transcript.json
tests/app/scenarios/sent-messages.json

# Root-level scratch files, by SHAPE rather than by name (2026-08-25).
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. On 2026-08-25 the root held _msgws_raw.txt,
# _msgws_full.txt, _messages_ui_dump.txt, _triage_tail.txt, _triage_tail2.txt
# and _orig_bytes.tmp -- ~90 KB of dumps from a live message-triage session --
# none of them ignored, so a single `git add -A` would have published them.
# Naming each one only ever catches the files someone already thought of, so
# the rule is the shape: a leading underscore at the repo root means scratch.
#
# Scoped to the root with a leading slash on purpose, so package sources like
# src/agent_friday/**/_internal.py are unaffected. Verified with `git ls-files`
# that nothing tracked matches. packaging/windows/build-installer.ps1 carries
# the same patterns so these never reach the installer payload either.
/_*
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
